            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0423" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 741.8215/37.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires at
                            London to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1569.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a note<hi rendition="#superscript">1</hi> which I have received from the
                    foreign office, dated the 31st ultimo, stating that Sir Edward Grey is informed
                    by the British consul general at Monrovia that the Sierra Leone-Liberia frontier
                    agreement has been ratified by the Government of Liberia. Sir E. Grey also
                    expresses <pb facs="0424" n="342" xml:id="pg342"/> thanks for the action taken
                    by this embassy and by the Department in facilitating the settlement of the
                    question.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
